arch: riscv: optionally put _isr_wrapper in .text

_isr_wrapper lives in .exception.entry, which the linker script keeps in
XIP flash and which zephyr_code_relocate() cannot move (it only handles
.text/.rodata/.data/.bss input sections). With a CLIC every interrupt and,
with RISCV_ALWAYS_SWITCH_THROUGH_ECALL, every context switch runs it; on
IPRO6S (XIP flash, ~7 traps per received Wi-Fi MPDU) its I-cache misses
cost several microseconds per trap. With CONFIG_RISCV_ISR_WRAPPER_IN_TEXT
(defined by the SoC/module that relocates it together with the hooks it
calls) it goes to .text, where it stays in flash unless relocated. vector.S
takes its address for mtvec, so it is kept by --gc-sections, and the
.balign below still gives mtvec its alignment. Without the option nothing
changes, so a patched tree still builds code that does not know about it.

Carried by the IPRO SDK through zephyr/patches.yml (west patch apply).

--- a/arch/riscv/core/isr.S
+++ b/arch/riscv/core/isr.S
@@ -134,7 +134,11 @@
 /*
  * Handler called upon each exception/interrupt/fault
  */
-SECTION_FUNC(exception.entry, _isr_wrapper)
+#ifdef CONFIG_RISCV_ISR_WRAPPER_IN_TEXT
+SECTION_FUNC(TEXT, _isr_wrapper)
+#else
+SECTION_FUNC(exception.entry, _isr_wrapper)
+#endif
 
 /* Provide requested alignment, which depends e.g. on MTVEC format */
 .balign CONFIG_RISCV_TRAP_HANDLER_ALIGNMENT
